From: niu-git
Subject: [PATCH] CMake: write GIT-BUILD-OPTIONS outside the BUILD_TESTING guard

Justification (see patches/README.md): tools/generate-script.sh,
tools/generate-perl.sh and tools/generate-python.sh source
$CMAKE_BINARY_DIR/GIT-BUILD-OPTIONS, and their custom commands are not gated
by BUILD_TESTING while the block that writes that file was. niu-git builds
with -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF, so a clean build failed in every generator with
"GIT-BUILD-OPTIONS: No such file or directory" - a reused build directory
hid it locally until CI ran on a fresh one.

--- a/contrib/buildsystems/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/contrib/buildsystems/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1147,6 +1147,16 @@ string(REPLACE "@MERGE_TOOLS_DIR@" "${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/mergetools" content "${c
 string(REPLACE "@PROG@" "${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/git-cvsserver" content "${content}")
 file(WRITE ${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/bin-wrappers/git-cvsserver ${content})
 
+# GIT-BUILD-OPTIONS is consumed by tools/generate-script.sh,
+# tools/generate-perl.sh and tools/generate-python.sh, and those custom
+# commands live outside BUILD_TESTING (see the shell/perl/python generation
+# blocks above). The block that writes it was inside, so a clean
+# -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF build failed in every generator with
+# "GIT-BUILD-OPTIONS: No such file or directory" (observed in CI; a reused
+# build directory hides it). Close the guard here and reopen it after the
+# file is written.
+endif()#BUILD_TESTING
+
 #options for configuring test options
 option(PERL_TESTS "Perform tests that use perl" ON)
 option(PYTHON_TESTS "Perform tests that use python" ON)
@@ -1245,6 +1255,7 @@ if(USE_VCPKG)
 endif()
 file(WRITE ${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/GIT-BUILD-OPTIONS ${git_build_options})
 
+if(BUILD_TESTING)
 #Make the tests work when building out of the source tree
 get_filename_component(CACHE_PATH ${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/../../CMakeCache.txt ABSOLUTE)
 if(NOT ${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/CMakeCache.txt STREQUAL ${CACHE_PATH})
